USER STORIES

US-S-01: As a registered user, I want to upload my notes, so that I can share my point of view on certain topics.

US-S-02: As a user, I want to search for posts using specific tags/topics, so that I can quickly find relevant content without scrolling through the entire library.

US-S-03: As a user, I want to download selected posts, so that I can access the content offline or keep a local copy for my personal use.

US-S-04: As a user, I want to rate posts, so that I can provide feedback and help other users identify high-quality content.

US-S-05: As a user, I want to access the main content library, so that I can browse, search, and manage my interactions with all available posts.

US-A-01: As an administrator, I want to create new tags, so that I can properly categorize new posts and maintain an organized library.

US-A-02: As an administrator, I want to review new posts, so that I can ensure the content doesn’t break community guidelines before it is made publicly available in the library.

US-A-03: As an administrator, I want to ban a user who breaks the TOS, so that I can prevent them from causing further harm or disruption to the platform.

US-A-04: As an administrator, I want to unban a user after a successful appeal, so that I can restore their account access if they have shown they are willing to follow the rules again or there was a mistake in the ban reason.

US-A-05: As an administrator, I want to accept or deny new user registrations, so that I can control who joins the platform and maintain a secure environment.

US-U-01: As a User, I want to log into the platform securely, so that I can access the application’s library and functions .

US-S-00 means its a user story from a student perspective
US-A-00 means its a user story from an adminstrator perspective
US-U-00 means its a user story from a universal (affects everyone) perspective

